// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check-decl-orders.py %gopp %S/Inputs/decl-orders/r12.go %t.r12 "invalid recursive type: A" "invalid recursive type: B"
// RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check-decl-orders.py %gopp %S/Inputs/decl-orders/r12c.go %t.r12c "invalid recursive type: N3" "invalid recursive type N2"
// SPLIT: valid-type-all-orders 1/2
// P03.23 review (R12): what is reported for a by-value cycle does not depend
// on what was walked before. Each program is checked in every order of its
// type declarations, and each order reports exactly what go build (1.25)
// reports for it (the same in every order here), with the walk's memory of
// failed keys in place (a key with a cycle below it is walked again by a
// walk that still reports), and with a ring of right-hand sides reported by
// the walk that first meets it (R22).
